    minutes the sentence lets pass, from what the scene established; the engine validates the
    answer, records it with its reason and confidence, and still decides whether the skip may
    stand (FR-CLOCK-8). -#}
{% block system %}
You estimate how much story time one sentence of a story lets pass. Use the activity the scene
established and the times the story established (when something started, how long it runs,
what time it is now); otherwise use ordinary knowledge of how long such things take. Count only
the time the sentence itself skips, from now. Give a short reason. When nothing tells you how
long it takes, give a low confidence. Answer only with a JSON object
{"minutes": <whole minutes, 0 or more>, "reason": "<one short sentence>", "confidence": 0.0-1.0}.
{% endblock %}
